      ],
      "text": "**Probably okay for a short, easy jog if you’re generally healthy—but the air isn’t great.** At about **12:40 p.m. local time on October 17**, readings ranged from **AQI 93 in George Town** to **101 in Bukit Mertajam** on the US AQI scale; a mainland Malaysian monitoring station reported **API 71** at 11 a.m. (Malaysia’s API and the US AQI are different scales.) ([iqair.com](https://www.iqair.com/air-quality/malaysia/penang))\n\nIf you run, keep it **short and light**, and stop if you develop coughing, wheezing, or unusual breathlessness. If you have asthma or another heart/lung condition—or you’re especially sensitive to haze—skip the strenuous outdoor run today. Moderate air quality can affect unusually sensitive people, and guidance advises them to make outdoor activity shorter and less intense. ([epa.gov](https://www.epa.gov/ozone-pollution-and-your-patients-health/patient-exposure-and-air-quality-index?utm_source=openai))\n\nCheck the reading for your specific part of Penang before heading out; it varies across the state.",
